{
  "dom_id": "step-q9346",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )+1\\cdot 1 & =0 \\\\ 3-3\\lambda -\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation.",
